---
/**
 * Work Preview Card — COMPONENT_INVENTORY.md §4.
 *
 * Purpose: the canonical preview of one Work Entry.
 * Responsibility: signpost a work so the visitor can decide to open it.
 * Appears on: Work Archive results (A-5), Related Work Strip (W-6), hub curated
 *   work (H-4), Service proof (S-4), Homepage pillar sections (M-4).
 * Notes (Inventory): "the single reusable 'Work card' everywhere; identical
 *   concept, identical structure." Variants are media treatment only.
 *
 * OWNERSHIP: Workstream A, single-owner file (TECHNICAL_ARCHITECTURE.md §23.3,
 * "Work Preview Card | A | touched by rendering *and* the field contract
 * simultaneously"). It lives at the component root rather than under
 * `homepage/` precisely so the next page to need it extends this file instead of
 * forking it.
 *
 * VARIANTS. Two, both media/caption treatment only — never a second
 * responsibility (Inventory §5: "Prefer extending an existing component over
 * creating a new one (variants, not new components)"):
 *   `focus`    the approved Homepage HiFi's focus-carousel card;
 *   `archive`  the approved Work Archive HiFi's archive card (Phase 5).
 * The archive's five-size vocabulary is NOT a set of card variants — sizing is
 * the grid cell's business, and it lives in the Results Grid.
 *
 * The archive variant serves both presentations of that grid: the curated views'
 * masonry catalogue and the Work Archive's project register, where the same
 * elements are composed as a full-width editorial unit (see work-archive.css
 * A-5a). The card does not know which — it renders identity, plate, caption and,
 * where the caller supplies one, a small preview of the entry's own gallery.
 *
 * REBUILT, NOT COPIED (§5.3). Markup and data attributes come from the Content
 * Model, never from HiFi markup: the metadata line renders Year + **Labels**
 * from the frozen vocabulary, where the HiFi prints an inconsistent mix of
 * Sector and Entry Type in the same slot. No `data-type`/`data-status` attribute
 * survives — those are the collapsed-taxonomy prototype debt §5.3 and R6 name.
 *
 * A CARD IS A LINK. The HiFi's `.proj` is an inert `<div>`. HOMEPAGE_WIREFRAME
 * M-4 permits individual cards to link to their Work Entry, and §14 makes every
 * interactive surface keyboard-operable — so the card is one `<a>`, reachable by
 * Tab, with its accessible name composed from the title and metadata it already
 * shows. Movement is never the only signal of interactivity (MOTION_NOTES.md:54).
 *
 * ── NO FOCUS CAPTION (resolved at I-3) ────────────────────────────────────
 * The approved HiFi reveals a one-line context caption on the focused card
 * ("Volum de beton asezat pe curba de nivel…"). It is not rendered, because no
 * upstream authority creates the content concept it would need:
 *
 *   - COMPONENT_INVENTORY.md "Work Preview Card" fixes this component's
 *     *Inputs:* "Work Entry preview (title, key facets, media)". No caption.
 *     §7 there is explicit that a new concept needs architectural justification
 *     and that "Visual variation alone is never sufficient reason".
 *   - `CONTENT_MODEL.md` §3 has no preview-caption field. The nearest candidates
 *     are `description` (Portable Text — truncating it would be derived
 *     editorial, and §19.2 governs its serialization) and `seo.description`
 *     (authored for search results, not for display). Neither is honest here.
 *   - `HOMEPAGE_WIREFRAME.md` M-4 lists Section Introduction · Work Preview Card
 *     · CTA Group, and nothing per-card beyond the card.
 *
 * A HiFi does not by itself create a CMS field. The slot is therefore absent
 * rather than filled with invented or repurposed copy. Adding a real
 * `previewCaption` is an owner + Content Model decision, flagged in the I-3
 * report; if it is taken, this component gains one element and B one field.
 */
import Plate from './media/Plate.astro';
import { localize } from '../lib/content';
import type { ImageAsset, Locale, WorkEntrySummary } from '../lib/content';
import { pillarLabel, projectLabelLabel, sectorLabel } from '../lib/i18n/vocabulary';
import { poolForPillar } from '../lib/dev/visual-media';

/**
 * One frame of the archive's project preview — see the `preview` prop.
 *
 * `image` is the entry's own gallery asset. `devKey` is non-null ONLY under the visual-QA
 * overlay, and only for a frame that stands in for a gallery the CMS does not hold; in a normal
 * build every frame carries a real image and a null key. The two are never both set.
 */
export interface PreviewFrame {
  readonly image: ImageAsset | null;
  readonly devKey: string | null;
  /**
   * Whether this frame's asset may fill its slot or must be contained on the plate tone.
   *
   * Decided by the caller, from the asset's own proportions against the slot the composition
   * gives it (`work-archive/preview.ts`). It reaches the card as an answer rather than as an
   * input because the card cannot know which slot a frame landed in — that is the sheet's
   * composition, and the sheet is a set. Absent means the caller expressed no preference, and
   * the stylesheet's default applies.
   */
  readonly fit?: 'cover' | 'contain';
}

interface Props {
  entry: WorkEntrySummary;
  locale: Locale;
  /** Destination — built by the caller from the frozen route map. */
  href: string;
  /**
   * `focus` variant — 1-based position, rendered as the HiFi's `pt·NN`
   * coordinate label. Decorative and `aria-hidden`.
   */
  index?: number;
  /**
   * `archive` variant — the coordinate label composed by the caller (`A·001`).
   *
   * The two approved HiFis label their cards differently: the Homepage numbers a
   * carousel position (`pt·NN`), while the Work Archive numbers an entry within
   * its pillar (`A·001` / `R·001`) — an identity, not a position, which must
   * therefore survive a re-sort. A card cannot derive the second from an index,
   * so the archive composes it in the Results Grid and passes it in. Both remain
   * decorative and `aria-hidden`.
   */
  coordinate?: string;
  /** Authored plate tone behind the photograph (see Plate.astro). */
  tone?: string;
  /**
   * Rendered already in focus. The carousel's runtime is an enhancement, so the
   * composition must be correct before it runs: one card is always "measured"
   * (VISUAL_DIRECTION_v2.0 §2.2), including with JavaScript disabled.
   * `focus` variant only.
   */
  focused?: boolean;
  variant?: 'focus' | 'archive';
  /**
   * `archive` variant only — the place line, already localized by the caller.
   * `CONTENT_MODEL.md` §3 puts Location on the Metadata axis ("mostly display"),
   * and the approved Work Archive HiFi prints it as the caption's fourth reading.
   * It is **not** a filter: the filter set is frozen at §23.5 and Location is not
   * in it.
   */
  place?: string | null;
  /** `archive` variant only — the hover/focus continuation cue. */
  openLabel?: string;
  /**
   * `archive` variant only — a small contact sheet of THIS entry's own gallery, composed by the
   * caller from `WorkArchiveItem.galleryPreview` (at most three, in the editor's order).
   *
   * WHY THE CALLER COMPOSES IT. The same reason `coordinate` and `place` are passed in: this
   * component's frozen input is a `WorkEntrySummary` (`COMPONENT_INVENTORY.md` "Work Preview
   * Card" — "Work Entry preview (title, key facets, media)"), and the summary carries no
   * gallery. Widening the summary would hand a gallery to the Related Work Strip, the hub and
   * the Service proof, none of which show one. The archive projection has the assets; the
   * archive's Results Grid selects from them; the card renders what it is given.
   *
   * Empty is the normal state and needs no fallback: an entry with no gallery is a complete
   * project unit made of its cover and its information. Nothing is substituted for an absence
   * (§10.4), the cover is never repeated to fill a frame, and no frame ever holds an image from
   * a neighbouring entry — every frame here came from this `entry`.
   */
  preview?: readonly PreviewFrame[];
  /**
   * `archive` variant only — the sheet's orientation signature (`ppp`, `pll`, `lll`, …),
   * published to the stylesheet as `data-preview-layout`.
   *
   * The card does not derive it, for the same reason it does not compose the sheet: it is a
   * property of a SET of images, and the Results Grid owns sets. See `work-archive/preview.ts`
   * for the rule and `work-archive.css` A-5a for what each token draws.
   */
  previewLayout?: string;
}

const {
  entry,
  locale,
  href,
  index = 1,
  coordinate,
  tone = '#c9c4ba',
  focused = false,
  variant = 'focus',
  place = null,
  openLabel = '',
  preview = [],
  previewLayout,
} = Astro.props;

/* Belt and braces against the projection's own bound: the composition below authors exactly
   four states (0 · 1 · 2 · 3) and a fourth frame would fall into none of them. */
const previewFrames = preview.slice(0, 3);

const label = coordinate ?? `pt·${String(index).padStart(2, '0')}`;
const title = localize(entry.title, locale);
/* STAGE 4: the caption's Entry Type reading became Project Labels. Entry Type was mandatory, so
   this slot always had a value; Labels are optional, so it renders only when the project carries
   one — a card for an unlabelled project simply has one reading fewer, never a placeholder. Both
   labels render when both are present. */
const labels = entry.labels.map((label) => projectLabelLabel(label, locale)).join(' · ') || null;
/* The archive caption's first reading — the pillar, carrying the blue signal
   exactly as the HiFi's `.pl-tag` does. Authored since Stage 5 (v3.1 §2). */
const pillar = pillarLabel(entry.pillar, locale);
/* The archive caption's fifth reading — Sector, from the axis the summary
   already carries (`WorkEntrySummary.sector`) through the closed vocabulary's own label.
   Rendered by the archive variant only. Single-valued and mandatory since Stage 6, so it is
   always present — no empty branch. */
const sector = sectorLabel(entry.sector, locale);

/* DEVELOPMENT ONLY — see `lib/dev/visual-media.ts`. Keyed on the entry rather than on the
   variant, so the same project shows the same picture on the homepage, its hub and the archive;
   that consistency is what makes the masonry rhythm readable in a screenshot pass. Inert without
   `DEV_VISUAL_MEDIA=true`, and never consulted when `entry.cover` is real. */
const devKey = `${entry._id}:card`;
const devPool = poolForPillar(entry.pillar, devKey);
---

{
  /*
   * ── THE ARCHIVE VARIANT (Phase 5) ────────────────────────────────────────
   * The variant this file reserved at I-3: "The archive's five-size masonry
   * variants arrive with the archive (Phase 5)". Same component, same
   * responsibility, same inputs — the Work Archive HiFi simply composes the
   * caption differently (title over a metadata line and a continuation cue,
   * rather than title beside a year), and its class names are that HiFi's own
   * (`.pl`, `.im`, `.cap`) so the CSS transcription stays legible against the
   * source. The size class and the grid cell belong to the **Results Grid**,
   * which is the component the Inventory makes responsible for presenting a set.
   *
   * The caption renders five INDEPENDENT axes — Pillar · Labels · Year ·
   * Location · Sector — where the HiFi prints a pillar tag beside an
   * inconsistent mix of Sector and Entry Type in one slot
   * (`WORK_ARCHIVE_IMPLEMENTATION_NOTES.md`:82 calls that out as the prototype's
   * collapsed taxonomy; §7.2 adopts "do not merge them" verbatim). They are set
   * on four rows — identity (`.cid`), title, place (`.pc`), metadata (`.d`) — so
   * the archive composition can give an entry's identity a column of its own
   * beside its photograph. No axis was added to the contract to do it: Sector is
   * already on `WorkEntrySummary`, and every label is the frozen vocabulary's.
   *
   * The identity row is the card's FIRST child, above the plate rather than
   * inside the caption, so the archive can rule it across the entire entry.
   * Reading order is unchanged in substance (the coordinate is `aria-hidden`
   * and the pillar tag simply now precedes the plate it labels).
   */
}
{
  variant === 'archive' ? (
    <a class="pl" href={href} data-work-id={entry._id}>
      {/* The identity line: the coordinate label and the pillar tag, set on
          one hairline-ruled row. Both readings existed already — the
          coordinate over the image (`.pid`) and the pillar at the head of the
          metadata line — and neither is new information. Moving the
          coordinate out of the plate is what lets an archive entry state its
          identity BESIDE its photograph rather than on top of it, which is
          the whole point of the featured composition below.

          RULED ENTRY (Direction A). It is a direct child of the card rather
          than of the caption, so its hairline spans the WHOLE project unit —
          photograph and caption together — instead of the text column alone.
          The rule is what makes one entry legibly one entry; the caption is
          only half of it. Identical for the lead and for every ordinary
          entry: the lead teaches the grammar, it does not have its own. */}
      <span class="cid">
        <span class="no" aria-hidden="true">
          {label}
        </span>
        <span class="pl-tag">{pillar}</span>
      </span>

      {/* The plate carries the hover on its own. The HiFi's growing blue mark
          (`.mk`) is gone: a 40px bar arriving inside the image frame is new
          visual structure rather than a state, and it was a second simultaneous
          blue signal beside the continuation cue's arrow. The element is removed
          rather than left inert, so nothing decorative and unstyled survives in
          the markup. `focus` variant's `.pmark` is a different device on a
          different composition and is untouched. */}
      <span class="im">
        <Plate image={entry.cover} locale={locale} tone={tone} devKey={devKey} devPool={devPool} />
      </span>

      <span class="cap">
        <span class="t">{title}</span>
        {place && <span class="pc">{place}</span>}
        <span class="d">
          {labels && <span>{labels}</span>}
          <span>{entry.year}</span>
          <span class="sc">{sector}</span>
        </span>
        {/* ── THE PROJECT PREVIEW — a glimpse inside, not a gallery ───────────
            Two to three of the entry's own gallery images, set small beneath its
            metadata. The archive is a signposting surface
            (`COMPONENT_INVENTORY.md`: "signposting previews… never in-depth
            projects"), so this is deliberately a contact sheet and not the W-2
            Gallery: no zoom, no Media Viewer, no captions, no coordinates. It
            says "there is more of this project" and routes to the project to
            show it.

            `aria-hidden`, and that is the accessible choice rather than a
            shortcut. The card is ONE link, already named by its title and
            metadata; every image inside it contributes to that one name, so
            three authored alt texts would append three sentences to the name of
            a link whose job is to say which project it opens. The same images
            are reachable, individually named and individually inspectable on the
            Work Entry the link leads to, which is where an alt text is a
            reading rather than noise. Nothing here is information a visitor can
            get only from this element. */}
        {previewFrames.length > 0 && (
          <span
            class:list={['gs', `gs-${previewFrames.length}`]}
            data-preview-layout={previewLayout}
            aria-hidden="true"
          >
            {previewFrames.map((frame) => (
              <span class="gf" data-fit={frame.fit}>
                <Plate
                  image={frame.image}
                  locale={locale}
                  tone={tone}
                  devKey={frame.devKey}
                  devPool={devPool}
                />
              </span>
            ))}
          </span>
        )}

        {/* The link is already named by its title and metadata; the cue would
            only repeat it into the accessible name. It is a visual affordance,
            and never the only signal of interactivity (MOTION_NOTES.md:54) —
            the whole card is the link, and focus-visible outlines it. */}
        {openLabel && (
          <span class="go" aria-hidden="true">
            {openLabel} <span class="ar">→</span>
          </span>
        )}
      </span>
    </a>
  ) : (
    <a
      class:list={['proj', focused && 'focused']}
      href={href}
      data-work-id={entry._id}
      aria-current={focused ? 'true' : undefined}
    >
      <span class="pimg">
        <Plate image={entry.cover} locale={locale} tone={tone} devKey={devKey} devPool={devPool} />
        <span class="pmark" aria-hidden="true" />
        <span class="pscan" aria-hidden="true" />
        <span class="pcoord" aria-hidden="true">
          {label}
        </span>
      </span>

      <span class="meta">
        <span class="t">{title}</span>
        {/* STAGE 4: Year + Labels replaces Year + Entry Type. Entry Type was mandatory so the
            separator was always earned; Labels are optional, so an unlabelled project shows the
            year alone rather than a trailing bullet. */}
        <span class="d">
          {labels ? `${entry.year} · ${labels}` : entry.year}
        </span>
      </span>
    </a>
  )
}
